<Base title="How we rank" description="How ReceptionistMatch ranks AI receptionists and answering services: by fit for your trade, call volume, hours and budget. Never by commission.">
<div class="page prose">
  <h1>How we rank</h1>
  <p>ReceptionistMatch is an independent buyer's guide to AI receptionists and live answering services for local businesses. We read every pricing page so you don't have to, then match the options to the way your business actually takes calls.</p>

  <h2>What decides a ranking</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your trade.</strong> A dental office, a plumber and a law firm need different things from a phone.</li>
    <li><strong>Calls a month.</strong> Per-minute and per-call pricing can flip which option is cheaper.</li>
    <li><strong>Hours covered.</strong> After hours only, or 24/7.</li>
    <li><strong>AI or live people.</strong> An AI receptionist and an answering service with real people are different products. We keep them apart.</li>
    <li><strong>Real monthly cost.</strong> Plan price plus the overage you are likely to hit.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What never decides a ranking</h2>
  <p>Commission. Some vendors pay us when you sign up through our links. That payout is not an input to any ranking or to our match quiz, and services that pay us nothing are listed whenever they fit. Every guide says which vendors pay us before the first link. The full list is on our <a href="/disclosure/">disclosure page</a>.</p>

  <h2>Where the facts come from</h2>
  <p>Prices and features come from each vendor's own pages. Every price links to the source and carries the date we checked it. When a vendor doesn't publish a price, we say so instead of guessing. When a price changes, the page changes.</p>

  <h2>What we don't claim</h2>
  <p>We tell you what we read and verified. We don't claim to have tested a service unless we really did, and we don't invent customers, quotes or numbers.</p>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>Spot a wrong price or an outdated feature? Email <a href="mailto:hello@receptionistmatch.com">hello@receptionistmatch.com</a>. A person reads every message.</p>
</div>
</Base>
